# Approach 1: Using Stack

# Complexity
- Time complexity: $$O(n)$$

- Space complexity: $$O(n)$$

# Code
```java []
class Solution {
    public int minAddToMakeValid(String s) {
        int stack_size = 0;
        int req_open_parenthesis = 0;

        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') {
                stack_size++;
            } else {
                if (stack_size == 0) {
                    req_open_parenthesis++;
                } else {
                    stack_size--;
                }
            }
        }

        return stack_size + req_open_parenthesis;
    }
}
```

# Approach 2: Without Using Stack

# Complexity
- Time complexity: $$O(n)$$

- Space complexity: $$O(1)$$

```Java []
class Solution {
    public int minAddToMakeValid(String s) {
        Stack<Character> st = new Stack<>();
        int req_open_parenthesis = 0;

        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') {
                st.push(c);
            } else {
                if (st.empty()) {
                    req_open_parenthesis++;
                } else {
                    st.pop();
                }
            }
        }

        return st.size() + req_open_parenthesis;
    }
}
```
